IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cma-types`
IMPORT `cma-definitions`
IMPORT `cma-offences`

-- Computer Misuse Act 1993 — GOAL 4: REACH AND PROCEDURE (ss 13-20).
--
--   "Does the Act reach this conduct; may the charges be amalgamated; which
--    court tries it; may it be compounded, and for how much; may compensation
--    be ordered; may the police arrest without warrant?"
--
-- Source: ../source/CMA1993.txt lines 541-667.

§ `Goal 4 — reach and procedure`

§§ `Territorial scope (s 13)`

-- s 13(1)-(2): the Act has effect "whatever the person's nationality or
-- citizenship, outside as well as within Singapore", and an offence committed
-- outside Singapore may be dealt with as if committed within. s 13(3): "this
-- Act applies if — (a) ... the accused was in Singapore at the material time;
-- (b) for the offence in question (being one under section 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 or
-- 8), the computer, program or data was in Singapore at the material time; (c)
-- the offence causes, or creates a significant risk of, serious harm in
-- Singapore; or (d) the offence is one under section 8A(1) or 8B(1)".
-- s 13(5): it is immaterial whether the harm is direct or the only or main
-- cause.
@ref s 13(1)-(5)
GIVEN o IS AN `Alleged offence`, t IS A `Territorial facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act reaches the conduct` o t IF
        t's `the accused was in Singapore at the material time`
    OR  (elem (`the provision of` o) (LIST "s 3", "s 4", "s 5", "s 6", "s 7", "s 8")
         AND t's `the computer, program or data was in Singapore at the material time`)
    OR  NOT t's `harm caused or significantly risked` EQUALS `no serious harm in Singapore`
    OR  elem (`the provision of` o) (LIST "s 8A", "s 8B")

§§ `Amalgamation of charges (s 14)`

-- s 14(1): "2 or more acts — (a) each of which is an offence under the same
-- provision in Part 2; (b) that involve the same computer; and (c) that are
-- committed in a period that does not exceed 12 months". s 14(2)-(3): one
-- charge, naming the computer and the dates between which the acts were
-- committed, "is treated as a charge of one offence".
-- FORK F2: the period runs from the first act to the last; it does not exceed
-- 12 months if the last act is on or before the same day of the month twelve
-- months after the first (the first day excluded, as in s 50(a) of the
-- Interpretation Act 1965). Revised 2026-10-07 after the independent pass.
DECLARE `Act charged` HAS
    `provision`      IS A STRING
    `computer`       IS A STRING
    `committed on`   IS A DATE

@ref s 14(1)-(3)
GIVEN acts IS A LIST OF `Act charged`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the acts may be charged as one offence` acts IF
    CONSIDER acts
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
            NOT null rest
        AND all (GIVEN x YIELD x's `provision` EQUALS first's `provision`) rest
        AND all (GIVEN x YIELD x's `computer` EQUALS first's `computer`) rest
        AND `the latest of` (first's `committed on`) `days` AT MOST `add months` (`the earliest of` (first's `committed on`) `days`) 12
        WHERE
            `days` MEANS map (GIVEN x YIELD x's `committed on`) rest

GIVEN d IS A DATE, ds IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest of` d ds MEANS
    CONSIDER ds
    WHEN EMPTY THEN d
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY more THEN `the earliest of` (IF e LESS THAN d THEN e ELSE d) more

GIVEN d IS A DATE, ds IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the latest of` d ds MEANS
    CONSIDER ds
    WHEN EMPTY THEN d
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY more THEN `the latest of` (IF e GREATER THAN d THEN e ELSE d) more

§§ `Courts (s 15)`

-- s 15: "A District Court or a Magistrate's Court has jurisdiction to hear and
-- determine all offences under this Act and, despite anything to the contrary
-- in the Criminal Procedure Code 2010, has power to impose the full penalty".
@ref s 15
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the courts that may try an offence and impose the full penalty` MEANS
    LIST "a District Court", "a Magistrate's Court"

§§ `Composition (s 16)`

-- s 16(1): "The Commissioner of Police or any person authorised by the
-- Commissioner may compound any offence under this Act that is prescribed as a
-- compoundable offence by collecting ... a sum not exceeding $3,000." Which
-- offences are prescribed is for regulations under s 16(2): an input.
@ref s 16(1)-(2)
GIVEN prescribed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the most that may be collected to compound, prescribed:` prescribed MEANS
    IF prescribed THEN JUST 3000 ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Compensation (s 17)`

-- s 17(1): on conviction the court "may make an order ... for the payment ...
-- of a sum to be fixed by the court by way of compensation to any other person
-- for any damage caused to the other person's computer, program or data by
-- the offence". "damage" here is the ordinary word: s 2(1) "damage" applies
-- "except for the purposes of section 17".
-- s 17(2): a claim for damages "is deemed to have been satisfied to the extent
-- of any amount which has been paid ... under an order for compensation, but
-- the order does not affect any right to a civil remedy for the recovery of
-- damages beyond the amount of compensation paid". s 17(3): recoverable as a
-- civil debt.
@ref s 17(1)
GIVEN convicted IS A BOOLEAN, harmed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a compensation order may be made, convicted:` convicted `, another's computer, program or data harmed:` harmed IF
    convicted AND harmed

@ref s 17(2)
GIVEN damages IS A NUMBER, paid IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the damages still recoverable in a civil claim, assessed at` damages `, compensation paid` paid MEANS
    IF damages GREATER THAN paid THEN damages MINUS paid ELSE 0

§§ `Investigation and arrest (ss 18-19)`

-- s 18: nothing in the Act prohibits a police officer, an authorised person
-- under s 39 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 or another duly authorised law
-- enforcement officer "from lawfully conducting investigations pursuant to the
-- powers conferred on him or her under any written law".
@ref s 18
GIVEN `a duly authorised law enforcement officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `lawfully investigating under a written law power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act does not prohibit the investigation, officer:` `a duly authorised law enforcement officer` `, lawful:` `lawfully investigating under a written law power` IF
    `a duly authorised law enforcement officer` AND `lawfully investigating under a written law power`

-- s 19: "Any police officer may arrest without warrant any person reasonably
-- suspected of committing an offence under this Act."
@ref s 19
GIVEN `reasonably suspected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a police officer may arrest without warrant, reasonably suspected:` `reasonably suspected` IF
    `reasonably suspected`

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

-- Nothing to compute: the long title, s 1, s 20 (the Minister may amend the
-- First and Second Schedules by order in the Gazette).
@ref long title; ss 1, 20
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "Long title: An Act to make provision for securing computer material against unauthorised access or modification, for preventing abuse of the national digital identity service, and for matters related thereto."
         "s 1: This Act is the Computer Misuse Act 1993."
         "s 20: The Minister may, by order in the Gazette, amend the First and Second Schedules."
